\ A default build (no --emit-runtime-image) embeds a metadata-only image whose
\ word bodies are empty. `floor` is a module word reachable only through the
\ hash-buried quotation dispatched at runtime, so the freezer never compiles
\ it, and the interpreted call would run its empty image body silently. The
\ build must reject this shape and direct the user to --emit-runtime-image,
\ which carries the module word's body.
use { floor: } "math" ;
3.7 H{ go: [ floor ] } go: @get call
.
